# I Am the Walrus, intro (figure 121.1)
# Pollack labels the Topline and Bassline only in the second system; they carry on through the last
# two, moving in parallel tenths ("the persuasive downward motion of bassline and upper voice").
# The bass notes are the chords (B A G F E D on the record); the top line's D over E makes E7, and
# its C over D makes D7. The D under the last system is implied by his IV7; he doesn't type it.
key A

system
caption 4 beats in the US, and 6 beats in the UK!
chords              | B{V-of-V} | - |

system
voice "Topline"     | D#5*2 C#5 F#5 | B4*2 A4 D5 |
chords "Bassline"   | B{V-of-V}*2 A | G*2 F |

system
voice "Topline"     | B4*3 C5 | D5 |
chords "Bassline"   | E{V7} | - |

system
voice "Topline"     | D5*3 B4 | C5 |
chords "Bassline"   | D{IV7} | - |
